# Derived vision model with the context window pinned.
#
# Why this exists
# ---------------
# qwen3-vl:4b served through Ollama allocates a 4096 token context window by
# default, the same allocation already found and corrected for llama3.2. For
# the text model that meant the front of a long transcript was silently
# discarded. For the vision model the consequence is different and worse.
#
# A rendered slide at 150 DPI costs a fixed 2303 prompt tokens, whatever the
# page contains. That leaves exactly 1793 tokens to generate in, and the
# probe confirmed the arithmetic directly: every truncated call reported
# completion_tokens 1793 and finish_reason "length", and 2303 + 1793 is 4096.
#
# qwen3 is a reasoning model. It thinks before it answers, and on a dense
# slide the reasoning alone ran to seven or eight thousand characters. The
# whole 1793 token allowance was spent thinking, the answer never started,
# and the call returned an empty string with no error. Across the C3
# instrumentation pass that happened on 49 of 111 slides, and in the
# extractor comparison behind the draft report it happened on 15 of 36.
#
# Why the window and not something else
# -------------------------------------
# The probe tested four alternatives on the same pages. Raising max_tokens
# to 2048 did not lift the limit, because the binding constraint is the
# window rather than a reply cap. Passing num_ctx through the request body
# was ignored, because Ollama's OpenAI compatible endpoint does not accept
# an options block. Disabling thinking through chat_template_kwargs and
# through the /no_think prompt convention were both ignored as well: the
# reasoning field came back just as long either way.
#
# A Modelfile is therefore the only control that actually binds, which is
# the same conclusion reached for the text model and for the same reason.
#
# 16384 is chosen to match the text model rather than for any property of
# its own. The measured need is roughly 2303 prompt tokens plus at most
# around 3500 for reasoning and answer together, so this is ample without
# being arbitrary, and using one figure across both models keeps the
# reproduction instructions short.
#
# Build it, once, from the repository root:
#     ollama create qwen3-vl-ctx16k -f Modelfile.vision
#
# Then set VISION_MODEL=qwen3-vl-ctx16k in .env, and confirm with
#     python probe_vision.py --deck "<any deck>" --pages 5,13
# where a fixed run reports finish=stop rather than finish=length.

FROM qwen3-vl:4b
PARAMETER num_ctx 16384
